Description: The 3D switch's Brazilian Portuguese label is "Ativar 3D" (ORDER 586), Daniel's decision of 2026-11-15: one idea keeps one name in every program and every language. The stereo layer and sView already read "Ativar 3D"; Haruna until now wrote "Ativar o 3D" for "Enable 3D" in patch 0006. Only this one word changes; pt (Portugal) is another language and stays as it is.
Author: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Origin: other, Sparky Stereo OS (ORDER 586)
Forwarded: not-needed (KDE takes translations through its teams)
Last-Update: 2026-11-15
Assisted-by: kimi-k3:cloud (Ollama) via Codex
---
--- a/po/pt_BR/haruna.po
+++ b/po/pt_BR/haruna.po
@@ -3765,7 +3765,7 @@
 
 msgctxt "@option:check"
 msgid "Enable 3D"
-msgstr "Ativar o 3D"
+msgstr "Ativar 3D"
 
 msgctxt "@info:tooltip"
 msgid "Shows 3D videos in 3D, whatever their packing, as full side by side views for the screen's 3D mode. When off, a 3D video is shown as it is stored."
